# The dbt job's own dependency set (pipeline/DBT.md's CI plan), compiled to
# requirements-dbt.txt with pip-compile on Python 3.12 - the version that job
# pins (pipeline-tests.yml's `dbt` job says why it still does). Separate from
# requirements.in on purpose: the pytest job never needs dbt, and the dbt job
# never needs rasterio/pillow/pmtiles.
#
# HASH-PINNED (pipeline/ELT.md decision 144, the maintainer's poll of
# 2026-10-09): the page dbt writes for ourhike.org/data/ comes from this
# install, and that page shares an origin with the app's signed-in session.
# So requirements-dbt.txt is compiled with --generate-hashes, which lists the
# sha256 of every file PyPI holds for each pinned version, every platform's
# wheels included (450 for the 20 pins, each set equal to PyPI's own file list
# on 2026-10-10), and every install passes --require-hashes, which refuses a
# download whose hash is not listed and a pin that lists none. Recompile from
# pipeline/, on Python 3.12, with the command the .txt's header records:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements-dbt.txt --strip-extras requirements-dbt.in
# .github/tests/test_dbt_install_is_hash_pinned.py fails a compile that drops
# the hashes and an install that drops the flag.
#
# duckdb is pinned identically to requirements.in's hand-written pin, and for
# the same ABI reason - the spatial extension is ABI-locked to the exact
# DuckDB version. Keep the two pins moving together. In this file it serves
# load_raw.py, which writes the fixture warehouse; dbt itself does not import
# it (next paragraph).
duckdb==1.5.5
#
# dbt v2, the full `dbt` distribution, one version everywhere with no
# dbt-core 1.x beside it (#1793 — Rebuild the data platform as dlt → dbt:
# seven contracted marts, a monthly refresh, published docs, and lighter phone
# downloads; decision 32 in its planning log). The maintainer chose it over
# the Apache-2.0 `dbt-oss`: "We get expanded features that way I believe".
# It is licensed under the dbt Product Licensing Agreement, not an open-source
# licence - its PyPI metadata carries no licence field at all. That agreement
# (§2.3) has dbt collect usage information unless the documented opt-out is
# set, which pipeline-tests.yml's `dbt` job and scripts/test.sh both set;
# §3.2 forbids switching off licence validation or anything else that talks
# to dbt's services, so nothing here does.
#
# dbt-oss 2.0.5 is the documented fallback: the same project files ran green
# on it, every CI step (measured 2026-10-01). Swapping back is this one line,
# a recompile, and scripts/test.sh's version check, which reads this file.
#
# v2 is a Rust binary, not a Python program, and neither distribution ships a
# database driver: on first use it downloads an ADBC driver for the profile's
# adapter from public.cdn.getdbt.com (docs.getdbt.com, "dbt v2 networking
# requirements"), for DuckDB a driver built on DuckDB 1.5.4, not the 1.5.5
# above. pipeline-tests.yml's `dbt` job says what is measured about that split.
#
# HOW IT INSTALLS, read from PyPI 2026-10-01, because it is not a wheel: PyPI
# holds one 3,291-byte sdist for 2.0.6 whose build backend (`_dbt_sa_build`,
# the same code dbt-oss's sdist carries) downloads the prebuilt wheel for this
# platform from public.cdn.getdbt.com/fs/wheels and refuses it unless its
# sha256 matches the sdist's own `assets.json`. So an install reaches dbt's
# CDN as well as PyPI. The wheels are cp311-abi3 (Linux x86-64 and ARM,
# macOS, Windows x86-64): any CPython >= 3.11, which is `Requires-Python`.
# The sdist's own sha256 is the one hash requirements-dbt.txt lists for dbt,
# and through `assets.json` it pins the wheel as well. On Linux x86-64 every
# hash-checked install built the manylinux_2_28_x86_64 wheel with the sha256
# assets.json names, af850377…b336 (measured 2026-10-10, Python 3.11 to 3.13).
dbt==2.0.6
#
# SQLFluff with its own jinja templater (pipeline/.sqlfluff). 4.3.0 is the
# newest release on PyPI, read 2026-10-01.
sqlfluff==4.3.0
